@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-adapter-il01`
IMPORT `il07-adapter-il02`
IMPORT `il07-adapter-il04`
IMPORT `il07-adapter-il08-ito`
IMPORT `il07-pipeline`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07: assertions EXPECTED TO FAIL. 4 of 4 fail, by design; check.sh and
-- encoding.json `expected_red` both carry the count. (Version 0.2.0 added R3.)
--
-- Each one states what a second source says, where a composed row says
-- otherwise. A failure here is a finding against a row (NOTES.md section 6,
-- RECONCILE.md section 3), not a defect of the composition, and no expected
-- value here is to be edited to make it pass.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — findings, expected to fail`

§§ `R1. The employee's deduction above the threshold: the Institute's 7%, the items' 4.67%`

-- Row IL-04, fork F4: Schedule J's column D items for 2026 sum to 4.67 above the
-- reduced collection threshold, while the printed totals row says 7.00 and the
-- National Insurance Institute's employees' rates page (IL-04 NOTES.md section
-- 7, fetched 2026-10-06, sha256 63457694...29aba) deducts "7" from the employee
-- above the threshold. IL-04 computes from the items; the Institute collects the
-- composite. At the household level (H3 of il07-tests.l4, a salary of 15,000 in
-- June 2026) the difference is 7,297 x (7% - 4.67%) = 170.0201 a month.
--   at the Institute's composite: 7,703 x 1.04% + 7,297 x 7% = 80.1112 + 510.79 = 590.9012
--   the net at it: 13,862.5571 - (590.9012 - 420.8811) = 13,692.537

`R1 household` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`  IS 2026
        `the month of the year`  IS 6
        `the earner`             IS `IL-07 earner` WITH
            `the earner's name`                                                              IS "Avi"
            `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS FALSE
            `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS YMD 1985 4 1
            `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS 15000
            `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
            `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
            `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
            `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
            `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
            `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
            `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
            `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS NOTHING
            `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse` IS JUST (`IL-07 couple` WITH
            `the earner's spouse` IS `IL-07 spouse` WITH
                `the spouse's name`                                                          IS "Batya"
                `the spouse is a woman`                                                      IS TRUE
                `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                IS 0
                `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`       IS FALSE
                `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
                `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`         IS TRUE
            `the earner is the registered spouse` IS TRUE
            `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS TRUE
            `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE)
        `the children of the household` IS LIST
            (`IL-07 child` WITH `the child's name` IS "Dana", `the child's date of birth` IS YMD 2023 8 20, `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE),
            (`IL-07 child` WITH `the child's name` IS "Eli", `the child's date of birth` IS YMD 2019 3 10, `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE)
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month` IS 626.0618

-- MENG'S RULING OF 2026-10-07: the capstone now reads column D at its printed
-- totals by default, so its default deduction and net for this household ARE
-- the Institute's (il07-tests.l4, H3: 590.9012 and 13,692.537), and these two
-- assertions, asked of the default, would pass. The finding stands against row
-- IL-04, which computes from the items, and against the items' reading the
-- capstone keeps as the alternative of its fork (NOTES.md K14). So from the
-- ruling the two assertions ask the items' reading by name; their expected
-- values, the Institute's, are unchanged. Row IL-11 is to put the same switch
-- inside IL-04; until then R1 is expected to fail.
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `R1 household` `, with further facts` `IL-07: no further facts` `, reading Schedule J column D as` `the sum of the items of the six deduction branches` EQUALS 590.9012
#ASSERT `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `R1 household` `, with further facts` `IL-07: no further facts` `, reading Schedule J column D as` `the sum of the items of the six deduction branches` EQUALS 13692.537

§§ `R2. Section 36A's half point in a separate calculation: IL-02 gives it where IL-01 declines`

-- ITO s 66(c)(4): "האשה תהא זכאית ל־½ נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36א" - the woman is
-- entitled to half a credit point UNDER S 36A. Row IL-01 encodes s 36A with the
-- reach of s 48A (the Minister may disapply the Chapter's credits to a foreign
-- worker; Regulations of 5775-2014 noted, not encoded) and declines for a
-- resident foreign worker. Row IL-02 restates the half point in its own record,
-- 0.5 for every woman in a separate calculation, without s 48A. For a resident
-- foreign-worker woman who claims a separate calculation, IL-01 declines and
-- IL-02 answers 0.5. The pipeline counts s 36A once, from IL-01 (RECONCILE.md
-- N7), so its answer declines; this assertion holds IL-02 to IL-01's reading.

`R2 couple` MEANS
    `IL-07 couple` WITH
        `the earner's spouse` IS `IL-07 spouse` WITH
            `the spouse's name`                                                          IS "Yoav"
            `the spouse is a woman`                                                      IS FALSE
            `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                IS 0
            `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`       IS TRUE
            `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
            `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`         IS TRUE
        `the earner is the registered spouse` IS FALSE
        `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS TRUE
        `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE

`R2 household` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`  IS 2026
        `the month of the year`  IS 3
        `the earner`             IS `IL-07 earner` WITH
            `the earner's name`                                                              IS "Galit"
            `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS TRUE
            `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS YMD 1988 9 15
            `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS 10000
            `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
            `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
            `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS TRUE
            `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
            `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
            `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
            `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
            `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS JUST 840
            `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse` IS JUST `R2 couple`
        `the children of the household` IS EMPTY
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month` IS 367.5618

-- IL-01 declines, as it should (this is the half of the pair that holds):
--   `IL-01: the credit points under section 36A for the earner` (R2's earner)
--   refuses "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in
--   this model" - asserted, satisfied, in il07-tests.l4 for the same earner (H18).
-- IL-02, held to the same reading, should decline too; it answers 0.5:
#ASSERT REFUSED (`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` `R2 household` `married as` `R2 couple`)'s `IL-02's half point under section 36A, by section 66(c)(4)` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `R3. Row IL-08's s 45A credit below the floor of s 45A(d)(1): its defect D187, on a household`

-- Added in version 0.2.0. ITO s 45A(d) (source lines 1725-1730): the total for
-- which credit is given to one who is not a beneficiary member "shall not exceed
-- the higher of" (1) the fixed amount, 2,268 for 2026, and (2) the lower of the
-- sums paid and 7% of qualifying income, within the proviso that survivors'
-- pension insurance is credited on no more than 1.5% of qualifying income.
-- R3's earner (H1 of il07-tests.l4: 10,000 a month, nothing insured) pays only
-- 5,000 of survivors' insurance. Qualifying income min(120,000, 116,400) =
-- 116,400; limb (2) after the proviso is 1.5% of it, 1,746; the higher is 2,268;
-- so 2,268 of the 5,000 is credited at 35%: 793.8 (row IL-08's own fork F5,
-- reading (i)). Row IL-08 answers 35% x 1,746 = 611.1 (its independent finding
-- D187). The pipeline declines this household (il07-tests-il08.l4, N4); this
-- assertion holds IL-08 to the text.
`R3 household` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`  IS 2026
        `the month of the year`  IS 3
        `the earner`             IS `IL-07 earner` WITH
            `the earner's name`                                                              IS "Amir"
            `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS FALSE
            `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS YMD 1985 4 1
            `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS 10000
            `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
            `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
            `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
            `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
            `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
            `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
            `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
            `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS NOTHING
            `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse` IS NOTHING
        `the children of the household` IS EMPTY
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month` IS 367.5618

`R3 payments` MEANS
    `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance` WITH
        `the earner's own contribution to a pension provident fund, each month`          IS 0
        `the employer's deposits to a pension provident fund for the earner, each month` IS 0
        `the part of the monthly salary that is insured income`                          IS 0
        `paid in the tax year for survivors' pension insurance`                          IS 5000
        `paid in the tax year for insurance of the earner's or the spouse's life`        IS 0

#ASSERT `IL-08: the credit under section 45A as row IL-08 computes it, for the earner, in` `R3 household` `, paying` `R3 payments` EQUALS 793.8
